From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp1: awb: program the measurement window every frame

The AWB measurement window is configured only on the first frame. On the
rk3566/rk3568 (ISP V21) the ISP does not apply the very first parameters
buffer, so the AWB window is never written to hardware: it stays zero, the
AWB measurement never completes, no statistics buffer is produced and the
capture pipeline stalls (video7/stats never dequeues, no frames delivered).

Send the AWB measurement configuration on every frame. It is idempotent
and cheap, and makes the rear camera stream through the hardware ISP.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/rkisp1/algorithms/awb.cpp b/src/ipa/rkisp1/algorithms/awb.cpp
index 0eb05c2b6..ed1df576d 100644
--- a/src/ipa/rkisp1/algorithms/awb.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/rkisp1/algorithms/awb.cpp
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ void Awb::queueRequest(IPAContext &context,
 /**
  * \copydoc libcamera::ipa::Algorithm::prepare
  */
-void Awb::prepare(IPAContext &context, const uint32_t frame,
+void Awb::prepare(IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const uint32_t frame,
 		  IPAFrameContext &frameContext, RkISP1Params *params)
 {
 	/*
@@ -232,10 +232,16 @@ void Awb::prepare(IPAContext &context, const uint32_t frame,
 	gainConfig->gain_red = std::clamp<int>(256 * frameContext.awb.gains.r(), 0, 0x3ff);
 	gainConfig->gain_green_r = std::clamp<int>(256 * frameContext.awb.gains.g(), 0, 0x3ff);
 
-	/* If we have already set the AWB measurement parameters, return. */
-	if (frame > 0)
-		return;
-
+	/*
+	 * The AWB measurement window and mode normally only need programming
+	 * once, on the first frame. On the rk3568 (V21) the very first
+	 * parameters buffer is not applied by the ISP, so a measurement block
+	 * configured only on frame 0 - the AWB window here - never reaches the
+	 * hardware: the window stays zero, no AWB statistics are produced and
+	 * the capture pipeline stalls waiting for stats. Program the
+	 * measurement configuration on every frame instead; it is idempotent
+	 * and cheap.
+	 */
 	auto awbConfig = params->block<BlockType::Awb>();
 	awbConfig.setEnabled(true);
 
-- 
